. New code should use a dedicated IdP/OAuth library for the AS. Example packages provide a demo with `better-auth`.\n./docs/faq.md:79:wanting to switch to `v2` and using SSE should migrate to Streamable HTTP.\n./docs/server-quickstart.md:40:> The MCP SDK also works with **Bun** and **Deno**. This tutorial uses Node.js, but you can substitute `bun` or `deno` commands where appropriate. For HTTP-based servers on Bun or Deno, use `WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport` instead of the Node.js-specific transport — see the [server guide](./server.md) for details.\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:8:# (2026-07-28). Several auth scenarios in this baseline (auth/iss-*,\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:9:# auth/authorization-server-migration, auth/enterprise-managed-authorization)\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:36:    # SEP-2468 (authorization response iss parameter): not implemented in the client.\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:37:    - auth/iss-supported\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:38:    - auth/iss-not-advertised\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:39:    - auth/iss-supported-missing\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:40:    - auth/iss-wrong-issuer\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:41:    - auth/iss-unexpected\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:42:    - auth/iss-normalized\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:43:    - auth/metadata-issuer-mismatch\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:44:    # SEP-2352 (authorization server migration): client does not re-register when\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:45:    # PRM authorization_servers changes.\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:46:    - auth/authorization-server-migration\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:49:    - auth/offline-access-not-supported\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:53:    # previously requested and newly challenged scopes on re-authorization; the\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:55:    - auth/scope-step-up\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:56:    # SEP-990 (enterprise-managed authorization extension): no fixture handler /\n./test/conformance/expected-failures.yaml:58:    - auth/enterprise-managed-authorization\n./test/conformance/README.md:16:pnpm run test:conformance:client -- --suite auth\n./test/conformance/README.md:19:pnpm run test:conformance:client -- --scenario auth/basic-cimd\n./test/conformance/README.md:69:- `src/authTestServer.ts` - Server with OAuth authentication for auth conformance tests\n./test/conformance/README.md:75:The `authTestServer.ts` is designed for testing server-side OAuth implementation. It requires an authorization server URL and validates tokens via introspection.\n./test/conformance/README.md:78:# Start with a fake auth server\n./test/conformance/README.md:80:  npx tsx src/authTestServer.ts\n./test/conformance/README.md:85:- Requires Bearer token authentication on all MCP endpoints\n./test/conformance/README.md:87:- Serves Protected Resource Metadata at `/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource`\n./examples/client/src/simpleClientCredentials.ts:4: * Example demonstrating client_credentials grant for machine-to-machine authentication.\n./examples/client/src/simpleClientCredentials.ts:6: * Supports two authentication methods based on environment variables:\n./examples/client/src/simpleClientCredentials.ts:22:import { Client, ClientCredentialsProvider, PrivateKeyJwtProvider, StreamableHTTPClientTransport } from '@modelcontextprotocol/client';\n./examples/client/src/simpleClientCredentials.ts:33:    // If private key is provided, use private_key_jwt authentication\n./examples/client/src/simpleClientCredentials.ts:37:        console.log('Using private_key_jwt authentication');\n./examples/client/src/simpleClientCredentials.ts:45:    // Otherwise, use client_secret_basic authentication\n./examples/client/src/simpleClientCredentials.ts:52:    console.log('Using client_secret_basic authentication');\n./examples/client/src/simpleClientCredentials.ts:64:    const transport = new StreamableHTTPClientTransport(new URL(DEFAULT_SERVER_URL), {\n./examples/client/src/simpleClientCredentials.ts:65:        authProvider: provider\n./CONTRIBUTING.md:121:pnpm --filter @modelcontextprotocol/examples-server exec tsx src/simpleStreamableHttp.ts\n./CONTRIBUTING.md:124:pnpm --filter @modelcontextprotocol/examples-client exec tsx src/simpleStreamableHttp.ts\n./examples/client/src/simpleOAuthClient.ts:8:import { Client, StreamableHTTPClientTransport, UnauthorizedError } from '@modelcontextprotocol/client';\n./examples/client/src/simpleOAuthClient.ts:15:const CALLBACK_PORT = 8090; // Use different port than auth server (3001)\n./examples/client/src/simpleOAuthClient.ts:19: * Interactive MCP client with OAuth authentication\n./examples/client/src/simpleOAuthClient.ts:20: * Demonstrates the complete OAuth flow with browser-based authorization\n./examples/client/src/simpleOAuthClient.ts:44:     * Opens the authorization URL in the user's default browser\n./examples/client/src/simpleOAuthClient.ts:49:        console.log(`🌐 Opening browser for authorization: ${url}`);\n./examples/client/src/simpleOAuthClient.ts:116:                    reject(new Error(`OAuth authorization failed: ${error}`));\n./examples/client/src/simpleOAuthClient.ts:118:                    console.log(`❌ No authorization code or error in callback`);\n./examples/client/src/simpleOAuthClient.ts:121:                    reject(new Error('No authorization code provided'));\n./examples/client/src/simpleOAuthClient.ts:131:    private async attemptConnection(oauthProvider: InMemoryOAuthClientProvider): Promise<void> {\n./examples/client/src/simpleOAuthClient.ts:134:        const transport = new StreamableHTTPClientTransport(baseUrl, {\n./examples/client/src/simpleOAuthClient.ts:135:            authProvider: oauthProvider\n./examples/client/src/simpleOAuthClient.ts:144:            if (error instanceof UnauthorizedErr