rs.\n./docs/migration.md:128:Use `StdioClientTransport` for local servers or `StreamableHTTPClientTransport` for remote servers. If you need WebSocket for a custom deployment, implement the `Transport` interface directly — it remains exported from `@modelcontextprotocol/client`.\n./docs/migration.md:140:import { StreamableHTTPClientTransport } from '@modelcontextprotocol/client';\n./docs/migration.md:141:const transport = new StreamableHTTPClientTransport(new URL('http://localhost:3000/mcp'));\n./docs/migration.md:144:### Server auth split\n./docs/migration.md:148:Authorization Server helpers (`mcpAuthRouter`, `OAuthServerProvider`, `ProxyOAuthServerProvider`, `authenticateClient`, `allowedMethods`, etc.) have been removed from the core SDK; new code should use a dedicated IdP/OAuth library. See the [examples](../examples/server/src/) for\n./docs/migration.md:149:a working demo with `better-auth`.\n./docs/migration.md:151:Note: `AuthInfo` has moved from `server/auth/types.ts` to the core types and is now re-exported by `@modelcontextprotocol/client` and `@modelcontextprotocol/server`.\n./docs/migration.md:163:const transport = new StreamableHTTPClientTransport(url, {\n./docs/migration.md:180:const transport = new StreamableHTTPClientTransport(url, {\n./docs/migration.md:337:### Resumability gating for unknown protocol versions (Streamable HTTP server)\n./docs/migration.md:339:The server-side Streamable HTTP transport enables resumability behavior introduced with protocol version `2025-11-25` — SSE priming events and the `closeSSEStream` / `closeStandaloneSSEStream` callbacks — based on the client's protocol version. Previously this was an\n./docs/migration.md:583:| `AuthInfo` (from `server/auth/types.js`) | `AuthInfo` (now re-exported by `@modelcontextprotocol/client` and `@modelcontextprotocol/server`) |\n./docs/migration.md:615:| `extra.authInfo`                                  | `ctx.http?.authInfo`                                                   |\n./docs/mig