otocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#communication-security',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1575:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1576:        note: 'These exercise the HTTP hosting/auth layer (mostly over real Express); the matrix transport arg is ignored, so they run as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1580:    'hosting:auth:as:redirect-uri-binding': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1581:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#open-redirection',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1583:            \"The bundled token endpoint rejects an authorization-code exchange whose `redirect_uri` differs from the one used at authorize; the bundled authorize endpoint rejects a `redirect_uri` not in the client's registered list without redirecting to it.\",\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1584:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1585:        note: 'These exercise the HTTP hosting/auth layer (mostly over real Express); the matrix transport arg is ignored, so they run as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1587:            'removed in v2: the bundled authorize and token endpoints no longer exist, so redirect_uri binding across authorize and token cannot be exercised.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1592:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1593:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting layer and session management; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1600:    'hosting:auth:query-token-ignored': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1602:        behavior: 'An access token presented in the URI query string is not accepted; the request is treated as unauthenticated.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1603:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1604:        note: 'These exercise the HTTP hosting/auth layer (mostly over real Express); the matrix transport arg is ignored, so they run as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1606:    'hosting:auth:as:authorize-requires-pkce': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1607:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#authorization-code-protection',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1608:        behavior: 'The bundled authorization endpoint rejects an authorize request that omits `code_challenge` with `invalid_request`.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1609:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1610:        note: 'These exercise the HTTP hosting/auth layer (mostly over real Express); the matrix transport arg is ignored, so they run as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1612:            'removed in v2: the bundled authorization endpoint no longer exists, so PKCE enforcement at authorize cannot be exercised.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1614:    'hosting:auth:as:verifier-mismatch': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1615:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#authorization-code-protection',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1617:            'The bundled token endpoint rejects an authorization-code exchange whose `code_verifier` does not hash to the stored `code_challenge` with `invalid_grant`.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1618:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1619:        note: 'These exercise the HTTP hosting/auth layer (mostly over real Express); the matrix transport arg is ignored, so they run as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1623:    'hosting:auth:as:code-single-use': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1626:            'An authorization code can be exchanged exactly once; a second exchange of the same code is rejected with `invalid_grant`. Enforced by the provider deleting the code on first use; the handler relies on `the stored authorization code` returning None.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1627:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1628:        note: 'These exercise the HTTP hosting/auth layer (mostly over real Express); the matrix transport arg is ignored, so they run as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1630:            'removed in v2: the bundled token endpoint no longer exists, so single-use authorization-code exchange cannot be exercised.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1636:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1637:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting layer; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1640:    // Client transport: streamableHttp\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1645:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1652:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1653:        note: 'This exercises the StreamableHTTP client transport directly; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1656:                note: 'On a 404 for an existing session the transport throws StreamableHTTPError (streamableHttp.ts:551) and never re-initializes — no session recovery is attempted.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1663:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1664:        note: 'This exercises the StreamableHTTP client transport directly; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements