ransport directly; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1754:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1755:        note: 'This exercises the StreamableHTTP client transport directly; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1760:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1761:        note: 'This exercises the StreamableHTTP client transport directly; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1767:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1771:                note: 'src/client/streamableHttp.ts error-wrapping code: SSE body-stream errors wrapped as new Error(`SSE stream disconnected: ...`) with no .cause, losing original instance/stack.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1776:    // Client auth\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1778:    'client-auth:401-after-auth-throws': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1780:        behavior: 'If the server still returns 401 after a successful authorization, the client fails instead of looping.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1781:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1782:        note: 'These exercise the HTTP hosting/auth layer (mostly over real Express); the matrix transport arg is ignored, so they run as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1784:    'client-auth:401-triggers-flow': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1785:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#protected-resource-metadata-discovery-requirements',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1786:        behavior: 'A 401 on a request triggers the OAuth authorization flow once.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1787:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1788:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1790:    'client-auth:403-scope-upgrade': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1791:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#step-up-authorization-flow',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1792:        behavior: 'A 403 with WWW-Authenticate triggers a scope-upgrade authorization attempt; repeated 403s do not loop.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1793:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1794:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1796:    'client-auth:as-metadata-discovery:priority-order': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1797:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#authorization-server-metadata-discovery',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1799:            'The client discovers authorization-server metadata by trying, in order, the OAuth path-inserted, OIDC path-inserted, and OIDC path-appended well-known URLs (with the root-path forms when the issuer URL has no path).',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1800:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1801:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1803:    'client-auth:bearer-header:every-request': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1804:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#token-requirements',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1806:            'Once authorized, the client sends the bearer token in the Authorization header on every HTTP request to the MCP server, never in the query string.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1807:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1808:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1810:    'client-auth:cimd': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1811:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#client-id-metadata-document',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1813:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1814:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1816:    'client-auth:client-credentials': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1819:            'A client-credentials provider obtains a token without user interaction and the resulting bearer token authorizes subsequent requests.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1820:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1821:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1823:    'client-auth:dcr': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1824:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#dynamic-client-registration',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1825:        behavior: 'The client performs dynamic client registration against the authorization server when no client_id is preconfigured.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1826:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1827:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1829:    'client-auth:invalid-client-clears-all': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1831:        behavior: 'An invalid-client or unauthorized-client error during authorization invalidates all stored credentials.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1832:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1833:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1835:    'client-auth:invalid-grant-clears-tokens': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1837:        behavior: 'An invalid-grant error during authorization invalidates only the stored tokens.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1838:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1839:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1841:    'client-auth:pkce:refuse-if-unsupported': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1842:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#authorization-code-protection',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1844:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1845:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1847:    'client-auth:pkce:s256': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1848:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#authorization-code-protection',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1849:        behavior: 'The authorization request includes a PKCE S256 code challenge and the token request includes the matching verifier.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1850:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1851:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1853:    'client-auth:pre-registration': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1856:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1857:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1859:    'client-auth:private-key-jwt': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1861:        behavior: 'The client can authenticate the client-credentials grant with a signed JWT assertion.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1862:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1863:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1865:    'client-auth:prm-discovery:fallback-order': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1866:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#protected-resource-metadata-discovery-requirements',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1869:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1870:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1872:    'client-auth:prm-resource-mismatch': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1873:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#authorization-server-location',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1876:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1877:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1879:    'client-auth:resource-parameter': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1880:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#resource-parameter-implementation',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1882:            'The client includes the canonical server URI as the resource parameter in both the authorization request and the token request.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1883:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1884:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1886:    'client-auth:scope-selection:priority': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1887:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#scope-selection-strategy',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1890:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1891:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1893:    'typescript:client-auth:state:verify': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1895:        behavior: 'SDK calls provider.state?.() and includes the returned value as the state parameter in the authorize URL.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1896:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1897:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1899:    'client-auth:token-endpoint-auth-method': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1900:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#token-request',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1901:        behavior: 'The client authenticates to the token endpoint using the auth method established at registration.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1902:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1903:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1905:    'client-auth:low-level:discover-and-exchange': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1908:            'The low-level auth helpers compose standalone: discoverOAuthProtectedResourceMetadata → discoverAuthorizationServerMetadata → startAuthorization → exchangeAuthorization, called directly (without the auth() orchestrator or an OAuthClientProvider), chain their outputs to inputs and yield valid OAuthTokens against a live AS.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1909:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1910:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1912:    'client-auth:middleware:with-oauth': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1915:            'withOAuth(provider, baseUrl) wraps a fetch: adds Authorization: Bearer from provider.tokens(); on 401 it runs the auth() flow (discovery/refresh) and retries once with the fresh token; a REDIRECT result or a second 401 throws UnauthorizedError.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1916:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1917:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1919:    'client-auth:private-key-jwt:static-assertion': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1922:            'StaticPrivateKeyJwtProvider authenticates the client_credentials grant by sending a caller-supplied pre-built JWT verbatim as client_assertion (jwt-bearer), with a fixed client_id so DCR is skipped — no per-request signing.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1923:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1924:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1926:    'client-auth:refresh:transparent': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1929:            'An access token the client considers expired is transparently refreshed before the next request, using the stored refresh token; the refresh request includes the resource indicator and the new token is persisted.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1930:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1931:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1933:    'client-auth:as-metadata-discovery:issuer-validation': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1934:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#authorization-server-metadata-discovery',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1936:            'The client rejects authorization-server metadata whose issuer does not match the URL the metadata was retrieved from (RFC 8414 section 3.3).',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1937:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1938:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1941:                note: 'discoverAuthorizationServerMetadata never validates that the returned issuer matches the authorization-server URL the metadata was fetched from (RFC 8414 section 3.3), so spoofed-issuer metadata is accepted and the OAuth flow proceeds to registration and redirect.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1945:    'client-auth:prm-discovery:no-prm-fallback': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1948:            \"When every protected-resource metadata probe fails, the client falls back to discovering authorization-server metadata directly at the MCP server's origin (the legacy 2025-03-26 path) rather than aborting.\",\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1949:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1950:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1959:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1960:        note: 'Exercises the client fetch middleware over HTTP; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1966:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1967:        note: 'Exercises the client fetch middleware over HTTP; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2010:            'A single server instance can serve streamable HTTP and the legacy SSE transport concurrently; clients on either transport can call the same tools.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2011:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2012:        note: 'This is an HTTP-specific compatibility flow; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs. The SSE half is hosted with SSEServerTransport from @modelcontextprotocol/server-legacy/sse.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2014:    'flow:compat:streamable-then-sse-fallback': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2017:            'When a streamable HTTP initialize fails with 400, 404, or 405, falling back to the legacy SSE client transport against the same server connects successfully.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2018:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2019:        note: 'This is an HTTP-specific compatibility flow; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2029:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2033:        note: 'This is an HTTP-specific flow requiring session management and a standalone GET stream; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2043:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2047:        note: 'This is an HTTP-specific flow requiring session management; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2049:    'flow:oauth:authorization-code-roundtrip': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2050:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2051:        source: 'https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/authorization#authorization-flow-steps',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2053:            'Connecting to a protected server walks the authorization-code flow end to end: the first attempt requires authorization, the code is exchanged, and a subsequent connection succeeds.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2054:        note: 'End-to-end authorization-code journey (401 → discovery → DCR → redirect → finishAuth → authorized reconnect); the individual mechanisms are covered by the client-auth:* requirements. This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer and OAuth client; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2057:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2064:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2067:        note: 'This is an HTTP-specific flow requiring session management; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2077:        transports: ['inMemory', 'streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2081:        note: 'This is a multi-hop proxy flow that should work across transports; restricted to inMemory and streamableHttp to avoid test matrix bloat.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2152:            \"createMcpHonoApp() hosts an McpServer over real HTTP: a StreamableHTTPClientTransport pointed at the served app completes initialize, tools/list and tools/call against a WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport mounted on the app's /mcp routes.\",\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2153:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2154:        note: 'This exercises the Hono hosting adapter over a real HTTP listener; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2160:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2161:        note: 'This exercises the Hono hosting adapter over a real HTTP listener; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2166:            'createMcpFastifyApp() hosts an McpServer over real HTTP: a StreamableHTTPClientTransport pointed at the listening Fastify instance completes initialize, tools/list and tools/call against a WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport wired to its /mcp routes.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2167:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2168:        note: 'This exercises the Fastify hosting adapter over a real HTTP listener; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2174:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2175:        note: 'This exercises the Fastify hosting adapter over a real HTTP listener; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2180:            'createMcpExpressApp() returns an Express app that, with a streamable HTTP server transport mounted on a POST route, serves a full initialize and tools/call exchange.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2181:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2182:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting layer; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2188:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2189:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting layer; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2250:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2251:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting layer; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2273:            'An HTTP-level failure from the server endpoint (non-2xx response that is not an auth retry) surfaces on the client as an SdkHttpError exposing the HTTP status code via .status.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2274:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2275:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting layer; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2277:    'client-auth:oauth-error:consolidated-class': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2281:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2282:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP auth layer against a mock authorization server; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2284:    'client-auth:authprovider:token-attached': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2287:            'An AuthProvider supplied to StreamableHTTPClientTransport has token() called before each request and the returned token is attached as an Authorization: Bearer header on the HTTP requests.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2288:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2289:        note: \"This exercises the HTTP client transport's auth hook; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.\"\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2291:    'client-auth:authprovider:onunauthorized-retry': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2294:            'When the server answers 401, the transport awaits AuthProvider.onUnauthorized() and retries the request once with the refreshed token; a second 401 (or a provider without onUnauthorized) surfaces as UnauthorizedError.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2295:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2296:        note: \"This exercises the HTTP client transport's auth hook; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.\",\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2299:                test: 'second 401 after retry surfaces as UnauthorizedError',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2300:                note: 'A second 401 after onUnauthorized() re-authentication surfaces as SdkHttpError (ClientHttpAuthentication) instead of the UnauthorizedError documented on AuthProvider.onUnauthorized().'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2304:    'client-auth:authprovider:oauth-provider-adapted': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2307:            'Passing a full OAuthClientProvider as authProvider still works: the transport adapts it internally and attaches its access token as the bearer token on requests.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2308:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2309:        note: \"This exercises the HTTP client transport's auth hook; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.\"\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2314:            'A reconnectionScheduler supplied to StreamableHTTPClientTransport is invoked with (reconnect, delay, attemptCount) when an SSE stream drops, and invoking the provided reconnect callback re-establishes the stream (replacing the default backoff timer).',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2315:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2316:        note: \"This exercises the HTTP client transport's reconnection path; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.\"\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2342:            'When a Streamable HTTP POST or connect receives a non-OK response, the transport rejects with an SdkHttpError whose .status property is the HTTP status code so callers can branch on 401/403/404/4xx.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2343:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2344:        note: 'This exercises the Streamable HTTP client transport directly; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2359:            'StreamableHTTPClientTransport exposes the negotiated session id via a readable .sessionId property after initialization so consumers can persist and display it.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2360:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2361:        note: 'This exercises the Streamable HTTP client transport directly; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2366:            'A sessionId passed to the StreamableHTTPClientTransport constructor is sent as the Mcp-Session-Id header from the first request onwards.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2367:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2368:        note: 'This exercises the Streamable HTTP client transport directly; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2374:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2375:        note: 'This exercises the Streamable HTTP client transport directly; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2401:    'client-auth:auth-helper:result-values': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2404:            \"The auth() helper resolves to the literal string 'REDIRECT' when user authorization is required and 'AUTHORIZED' when tokens were obtained, and consumers branch on these exact values.\",\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2405:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2406:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2408:    'client-auth:refresh:typed-errors': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2411:            'Token refresh and authorization-code exchange failures surface as typed OAuth error classes (e.g. InvalidGrantError, InvalidClientError, ServerError) so consumers can decide between re-auth and hard failure.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2412:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2413:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2416:                note: 'changed in v2: the per-code OAuth error subclasses were consolidated into the single OAuthError class (carrying the machine-readable code), so refresh and exchange rejections are OAuthError rather than InvalidGrantError, InvalidClientError, ServerError, etc.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2420:    'client-auth:no-tokens:no-auth-header': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2423:            \"When the OAuth provider's tokens() returns undefined the transport sends no Authorization header and the resulting 401 re-enters the auth flow, and a token response without refresh_token leads back to a full authorization-code flow on expiry rather than a refresh attempt.\",\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2424:        transports: ['streamableHttp'],\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2425:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting/auth layer; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2427:    'client-transport:sse:401-unauthorized-code': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2430:         